{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0259","billNumberShort":"H.B. 259","billNumberLong":"HB0259S06","fileNumber":"2026FL0920","shortTitle":"Parental Access to Children's Medical Records Amendments","currentSubVersion":"6","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"PETERM","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Petersen, Michael J.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"BRAMMB","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Brammer, Brady","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to parent access to a minor's medical record.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>specifies that a parent has the right to access their child's medical record;<hr><ltbullet>requires a health care facility to ensure that a child's parent has access to the child's electronic health record unless certain circumstances are met;<hr><ltbullet>requires an electronic medical record system vendor to ensure a health care facility can provide access to parents;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes the attorney general's office to bring enforcement actions; and<hr><ltbullet>requires a health care facility to provide medical records free of charge under certain circumstances.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Christopher Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Sean C. Faherty","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"XGDJWNROPI","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-14 13:31:13.740","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-14 13:31:13.740","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":""